From: performance lane
Subject: [PATCH] suppliers screen: score the matched pool, not the whole
 directory

Applies to: f2a61a93c (farq repo; Frontend/src/pages/ConstructionPage.tsx is
clean at that revision, though it carries another lane's uncommitted work in the
shared tree — this patch was built and verified in a worktree).

WHY
---
The suppliers screen derives فرق's nominations with
autoSelectSuppliersForRequest(supplierPool, …). supplierPool folds in the entire
catalog directory, because the browse payload carries every active supplier and
the buyer must be able to search all of them (`searchable={knownSuppliers}`).

But a directory row arrives with no product_match, so it cannot clear the
evidence gate and cannot win a nomination. Scoring it is work with a known
answer, and the cost is linear in the size of the directory — which is why this
degraded as the directory grew to 11,727 rather than because any screen changed.

Measured against the production directory:

    families in the order      full pool (11,727)   matched rows only
    4  (short-form booklet)            82 ms                 1 ms
    33 (wide tender)                  919 ms                10 ms

That is a blocking main-thread recomputation, and it re-runs on every arrival at
the screen, because the suppliers/match effect is keyed on `screen` with no
already-loaded guard and its response replaces matchedSuppliers.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE
-----------------------
Who gets nominated. Verified against the production directory across 37
distinct families (a 4-family doors/gates/glass booklet and a 33-family tender
spanning tiles, concrete, electrical, plumbing, fire and HVAC): identical
nominations — same supplier ids, scores, grades and preapproved flags — and
identical state, qualifiedCount and preapprovedCount, 37/37. The only field that
differs is `rejected`, which gets shorter: the directory rows that used to be
scored and refused are no longer scored.

It also does not change what the screen can search. supplierPool and
knownSuppliers are untouched, so the buyer still searches all 11,727. This is
deliberately not the `include_suppliers=false` change: the live API already
honours that parameter, but passing it would shrink the searchable directory to
the matched rows, and fewer selectable candidates was already refused.

TEST
----
Frontend/src/lib/nominationPool.test.ts with real production rows for one
family: adding bare directory rows to the pool changes no nomination, and no
bare row is ever nominated. The first assertion is guarded against vacuity — it
requires the family to nominate somebody, which caught a bad fixture while this
was being written.

Suites re-run on the patched worktree: SupplierSelectionByMaterial 27,
SupplierSelectionExperience 15, nominationPool 2 — 44 passed. tsc clean.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM
------------------------
It is not established that this is the whole of the owner's navigation
slowness. It is measured waste on the screen he was on, removed with proof. The
React render and commit time for a full booklet's rows was not measured — that
needs a Performance trace from his browser, which I could not capture without
his session.

